## Who you write for

The owner, who has **not** read the code, the design, the log or any ruling,
and will not. They know their project, not this cycle.

- Every sentence stands alone. Introduce a thing before you lean on it; say a
  term from the design or the code in plain words the first time, or do not
  use it. A sentence the reader cannot follow without opening another
  artifact is a failed sentence — the tell is a design noun (a section
  number, a mechanism's internal name, a slug) used as if the reader knew it.
- Consequence before process: what this means for the project, in one
  sentence, before where it came from.
- Short. Shorter is better; a page is the ceiling.
